ter I ever saw, I reckon. It turned out one of his own men had cooked up the whole joke and never told a soul. I felt ashamed for being taken in, but I wouldn’t have been in that ring‑master’s shoes, not for a thousand dollars. I don’t know; there may be bullier circuses than that one, but I’ve never run into them yet. Anyway, it was good enough for me, and wherever I encounter it, it can have all of my custom each time.\n\nThat night we had our show; but there weren’t even twelve people there—just enough to cover expenses. They laughed the whole time, which made the duke angry; and everyone left before the performance ended, except for one boy who fell asleep."
